"""KMR2x1NGLFS — C&K (Littelfuse) KMR2 micro-miniature SMT tactile switches, no ground pin.

Selector package for the KMR2 series silver-contact, no-ground-pin (NG),
lead-free silver-plated (LFS) variants. All four variants share the same
4.2 x 2.2 mm body (4.6 mm over the gullwing leads), 1.9 mm high SMT
package, footprint, and pinout; they differ only in actuation force (and
rated operating life). Select by `actuation_force`.

 MPN          | Force        | Travel         | Operating life
 KMR211NGLFS  | 1.2 N (120g) | 0.20 ± 0.1 mm  | 200,000 cycles
 KMR221NGLFS  | 2 N (200g)   | 0.25 ± 0.1 mm  | 200,000 cycles
 KMR231NGLFS  | 3 N (300g)   | 0.25 ± 0.1 mm  | 150,000 cycles
 KMR241NGLFS  | 4 N (400g)   | 0.30 ± 0.1 mm  | 100,000 cycles

Electrical (silver contacts): SPST normally-open momentary, 32 VDC /
50 mA / 1 VA max, 1 mA min, contact resistance ≤ 100 mΩ, bounce ≤ 3 ms,
IP40, -40 °C to +85 °C.

Pinout: the datasheet "Electrical Diagram" (NG version) shows terminals
1 & 4 internally bonded as one pole and 2 & 3 as the other, with the
momentary contact between the poles. The symbol stacks the bonded pairs,
so the public API is just the two poles `P1` and `P2`; all four pads are
connected through the stacked pins.

Footprint follows the datasheet recommended NG land pattern (5.0 mm outer
/ 3.2 mm inner span, 0.9 x 1.0 mm pads on a 1.61 mm lead pitch). F.Fab draws
the 4.2 x 2.2 mm datasheet body; the actuator is simplified to a 2.2 mm circle
rather than the datasheet's 2.11 mm-wide oval.

3D model: KiCad's `SW_Push_1P1T-SH_NO_CK_KMR2xxG` STEP from kicad-packages3D,
embedded and aligned to this land pattern with no offset (its lead centres are
the same +/-2.05, +/-0.8 mm as these pads). It is the G-variant model, but it
carries only the four corner gullwing leads - no ground tab - so it represents
the NG part correctly, and it reproduces the 4.6 mm lead span, the 1.9 mm
actuator height and the ~2.1 x 1.3 mm oval actuator from the datasheet drawing.
It is 2.8 mm across the width where the datasheet gives 2.2 mm, i.e. 0.3 mm
oversize per side - conservative for clearance checks, but do not treat it as a
mechanical master. This replaced a featureless 4.82 x 2.8 x 2.1 mm block model
that had no actuator and was wrong on both length and height; the distributor
model could not be re-fetched (provider returns HTTP 500), and every other
source for this part is login-gated.

Not covered here: G variants (extra ground pin, different footprint),
gold-contact (KMR2x3...LFG, 10 mA max) and ULC low-current options. Add
them as separate symbols/packages if needed.
"""

actuation_force = config(
    str,
    default="1.2N",
    allowed=["1.2N", "2N", "3N", "4N"],
    help="Actuator operating force.",
)

P1 = io(Net)
P2 = io(Net)

_FAMILY = {
    "1.2N": "KMR211NG LFS",
    "2N": "KMR221NG LFS",
    "3N": "KMR231NG LFS",
    "4N": "KMR241NG LFS",
}

_mpn = _FAMILY[actuation_force]

Component(
    name="SW",
    symbol=Symbol(library="KMR2x1NGLFS.kicad_sym", name=_mpn.replace(" ", "")),
    part=Part(mpn=_mpn, manufacturer="C&K"),
    pins={"1": P1, "2": P2},
)
